   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/activity-7522266457137754112-BipG",
   "text": "No game engine. No game code. Every frame a probabilistic guess.\n\nTwo years ago, Decart and Etched released Oasis, which Decart calls the first playable open-world AI model. A Diffusion Transformer predicts each frame from keyboard and mouse input, trained on millions of hours of Minecraft footage.\n\nDecart open-sourced the code and weights of a smaller model, and by its CEO's account traffic nearly took the site down within a day.\n\nThe bet kept paying off. Decart raised $100M in August 2025 and $300M in May 2026, over $450M in total, and now describes its work as real-time world models. Google DeepMind's Genie, World Labs' Marble and Yann LeCun's AMI Labs are chasing the same idea.\n\nWould yo",
